  "_about": "The coverage gate's shared FGD bases (etest/coverage.py, etest/code_paths.py). A key of one of these bases is counted on every class that inherits it. A test on one class credits the key on the other classes of the base only when their C++ class keeps the base's code for it: a class whose own code replaces a method in the key's list (its override never calls the ancestor's), or never reaches a method in needs_call, needs its own test or an exemption. cpp: the base's C++ class. every_key: methods every key goes through (an override counts only when it does not call the ancestor's). keys: per FGD key (lower case), or key=value for one choice value, the methods its effect goes through. uses: per key (lower case, without a value), names (helpers, members) an override may use to apply the key itself: an override whose body uses one keeps the key's path (it counts as extending). own_cases: per key, per method, case labels (C++ case names) whose own handling in an override that calls the ancestor's still counts as the class's own code (a GetSchedule that decides MONSTERSTATE_ALERT itself, before the base's code reads the key). parts: the FGD base classes a base is built from (its keys are defined there; they count as the base's).",
